     "type": "teaming_up",
     "status": "proposed_only",
     "kind": "cross_section_trade",
     "sections": [
      "S2_thermal_testing",
      "S5_customer_disclosure"
     ],
     "excerpt": "The current v16 retains the 5% corrective-action trigger without an automatic sales ban, and the 8/100,000 threshold prompts regulator review rather than automatic recall. ... negotiators can sign v16 if satisfied.",
     "comparison": "S2 does not require sales to stop above 5% (weaker than the answer key's must-stop after bounded remediation) and S5 leaves recall to regulator discretion without a mandatory numeric recall (weaker than the acceptable range). Each side keeps the section that benefits it weakened in exchange for the other's, so this is a cross-section package below the acceptable range."
    }
