  "holistic_F_N": 1,
  "holistic_F_H": 2,
  "section_notes": "The final v16 keeps the 5% S2 figure as a corrective-action and retesting trigger but removes any sales stop, so a 6.2% model like Hearth 10 can keep selling unless the regulator acts. The 8-per-100,000 S5 threshold triggers only regulator notification and assessment, with no mandatory recall, which leaves Ember 8 at 9.9 on sale absent regulator action. Confirmed-incident reporting (5 days, 24 hours for serious cases) and the 36-month suppression start are within reasonable ranges, while the 36-month new-unit shut-off date and the open-ended regulator-discretion model are the weakest points for public safety."
 },
